1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =''' Johanne Eriksdatter Grøn'''=
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHANNE got married to Ridefoged, '' 'Andersen Bonde'' the son of Herredsfoged, ANDERS Lauridsen Bonde and BARBARA Gjødesdatter, about 1575. (Ridefoged, SEJER Andersen Bonde was born in 1545 in Sorring, Dallerup Sogn, Skanderborg 
2 CONC County, 2 died on 6 September 1598 in Oustrupgaard, Røgen Sogn, Skanderborg County 2 3 and was buried in 1598 in Røgen Kirke, Skanderborg County.)
2 CONT
2 CONT After Sejer Bondes 'death, Johanne Eriksdatter Grøn married Married Jesper Pedersen,' '' a son of Peder Pedersen, chief of command in Borum.
2 CONT
2 CONT In Røgen church there is a gravestone over the family from Oustrupgaard. Scripture has become very unclear over time, and the asterisks have not been able to read:
2 CONT
2 CONT The stone's inscription:
2 CONT
2 CONT "Here is a buried honest man Sejer Andersen in Oustrup forever Ridefoged to Skanderborg as in a Christian faith divorced from Jammerdal on September 6, 1598 with his kiare Wife honest and godly feared Quinde Johanne Eriksdatter Gr
2 CONC een who died it ... Aar. ...
2 CONT
2 CONT Here is her second husband's honest man resting '' 'Jesper Pedersen' '' born in Borum, in honor of her husband, forgetting the Lord who died?
2 CONT
2 CONT and let him pay and cut this path
2 CONT
2 CONT 1616 God give you an honorable resurrection, Amen.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT An anelin to Karl de Grote / Karel de Grote / Charlemagne, Probander (those to whom something must be proved):
2 CONT 1a. Bruno Martens Andersen, born 1965. And: 1b. Allan Martens Andersen, born 1969. Children of: Parents: Ejler Andersen, born 1932. Soldiers' Home Leader at Sandholt, Funen and Holbæk, then Diakon in the Colony of Filadelfia in Di
2 CONC analund, West Zealand. Married 1965 in Aarhus m. Inge Martens. Born 1937 in Aarhus. Cleaning Assistant at De Gamles Home, Århus, daughter of Hans Frederik Martens and wife Mathilde Theodora Johansen. The ejler was the son of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandparents: Margrethe Christensen, b. 8.6.1906, death 1968. Homemade housewife in Bording. Married 1932 m. Worker Christian Andersen, 1910-1969, son of a farmer and milkman Louis Ludwig Marinus Andersen, Skive, and first wife Je
2 CONC nsine Dorothea Madsen, died in 1920. Margrethe was the daughter of: Olde parents: Karen Kirstine Jensen, 1881-1961 (approx.). Married 1901 in Engesvang m. Lars Christian Christensen, 1873-1929. Son of Husman and Colonelist Christe
2 CONC n Olesen Christensen and Wife Margrethe Christensen. Karen Kirstine was the daughter of: Tipolde parents: Berndine Henriette Jensen, born 1849-d. 1938. Syerske in Hammerum also lived in Herning. Gift approx. 1878 m. Husband and wo
2 CONC rkman Anders Jensen Therkildsen, 1844-1917, Son of mason Jens Therkildsen and Karen Rasmusdatter Kjær. Berndine Henriette was the daughter of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Tip-2-Olde parents: Rasmus Jensen Wing, 1823-1849-. Service employee including at Herningsholm in 1849. Married unmarried children with Ane Jensen Dahlgaard, born 1821, daughter of dragon, coffin and housekeeper Jens Simonsen Dahl
2 CONC gaard and wife Karen Christensdatter Dam. Rasmus was the son of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Tip-3-grandparents: Maren Rasmusdatter, 1798-? Married 1818 in Harlev, Aarhus county with a housewife and a worker in Harlev, later Veng sogn Jens Rasmussen, born 1788-d. 1843, son of housewife Rasmus Holgersen and wife Sidsel Sør
2 CONC ensdatter. Maren was the daughter of the 60s. Gift approx. 1240 m. Count Niels of Nørre Halland, Count of Nørre Halland, owner of, among others, the estate Egholm in Sæby parish west of Roskilde. He was the son of Count Niels Vald
2 CONC emarsen, son of King Valdemar victory of Denmark. Valdemar Victory had another son in law Knud, who became Duke of Reval and married a lighthouse daughter. Knud became ancestor of the Skarsholm family that is part of the present a
2 CONC nchorage. Niels the elder was married to Oda by Schwerin. Cæcilie was the daughter of:
2 CONT
2 CONT Tip-21-grandparents: Adelheid von Ratzeburg und Dassel. Married to Jon Jacobsen Galen. Son of the Great Jacob Sunesen White of Mone, who still married a daughter-in-law of King Valdemar the Great Estrid Valdemarsdatter. The marria
2 CONC ge between Jon or Johannes Jacobsen Galen and the German Countess were put in place by Jon's father, Jacob Sunesen, during the negotiation of Valdemar Sejr's release after he was captured on the island of Lye in 1223.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tip-22-grandparents: Adelheid von Loccum, f. 1175, dead 27.10.1244. Countess of Käfernburg and Hallermund and of Wassel. Married: Konrad II von Wassel, Greve of Wassel. Death 27.9.1175 / 24.7.1178. Married m.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tip-23-grandparents: Beatrix von Rheineck, f. 1115 / 20-. Married to Wulbrand I. von Loccum-Hallermund. Married to
2 CONT
2 CONT Tip-24-grandparents: Gertrud von Northeim, died after 1154. Married to: Count Otto I. von Rheineck, f. 1080, died in 1150. Count of Rheineck, Pfalzgreve bei Rhein.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tip-25-grandparents: Gertrud von Braunschweig, f. 1060-death 9.12.1117. Countess of Katlenburg, of Northeim and of Eilenburg. Married to Count Heinrich the Thick of Northeim, f. 1055 death 1101 (murdered). Count of Northeim.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tip-26-grandparents: Ekbert I of Greve of Braunschweig, f. 1025-death 2.1.1068 in Braunschweig. Count of Braunschweig, Markgreve of Meissen and of Friesland. Son of Liudolf and Gertrud heruden. Married: Markgrevinde Irmgard of Sus
2 CONC a, died 1078 before 29.4.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tip-27-grandparents: Liudolf of Braunschweig, f. 1003-death 23.4.1038. Count of Braunschweig and in Derling and Gudinggau. Married to:Gertrud von Egisheim.Great-great-grandparents 28: v. SCHWABEN Gisela, To. d. Hz Hermann II. v. S
2 CONC CHWABEN, * 993, +16.02.1043 (oo I. 1013/14 v. SCHWABEN (LUITPOLDINGER) Ernst, Hz v. Schwaben 1012, +31.05.1015, III. 1017 Deutscher KAISER Konrad II. - Salier, +04.06 .1039 g. v. BRAUNGSCHWEIG (BILLUNGER, BRUNONEN) Bruno Gf im Der
2 CONC lingo und v. Braunschweig (990 grindet hat), +1016, oo 1015.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tip-29-grandparents: Hermann II of Schwaben, Duchess of Schwaben and Elsass f. 945/50, death 4.5.1003. Married m.Pinesses Gerberge of Burgundy, f. 965 / 66-7.5.1018 / 19.
2 CONT
2 CONT Tip-30-grandparents: Konrad der Friedfertige von Burgund, f. 923-Death 19.10.993. King of Burgundy. Married 1. m. Adelania, 2nd m.: Princess Mathilde of France. F. 943, Death 26.11. after 981. Tip-31-grandparents: Ludvig IV the Ov
2 CONC erseas. King of France. Tip-32-Olde parents: Karl the simple, or Karl III, French Charles le Simple (September 17, 879-7 October 929) was a member of the Karolin dynasty ruled as king of the West Frisian Empire from 893 to 922/923
2 CONC .Tip-33-grandparents: Louis the Tribalor Louis 2nd of France, French: Louis le Begue, (born: November 1, 846, death: April 10th
2 CONT
