2 CONC  Judge Jesper Pedersen, his wife, Johanne Grøn and her first husband, Sejer Andersen, Oustrup, bailiff of  Headstones. 1) Half Figure stones (Fig. 31), 1616 set by  former district bailiff in the works, Jesper Pedersen44  (see. P.
2 CONC  3545) of himself, his hustru Johanne  Grøn and his first husband Sejer Andersen.  The inscription mentions first Seier Andersen in  Ovstrvp, formerly bailiff to Skanderborig,  as 'afskildis from this vale of tears' 6 sept.  1598 
2 CONC and is buried here with his wife Iahin (!)  Green, † •. "Here at resting hindis second  hosbvnd 'Iesper Pedersen, b. In Borvm, formerly  herredsfoged i Giern township, † •' oc left hand  pay for oc vdhvgge this path 1616. GVD gifv
2 CONC e  dennom all one ærefvld resurrection Amen."  The great and velhugne, light gray limestone,  218xl65xca. 10 cm, has a centerpiece kartoucheindrammet,  rectangular box with the inscription recessed  capital letters. The stone fram
