1 OCCU Ridefoged på Skanderborg slot
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Sejer Andersen Bonde, Oustrupgaard==
2 CONT
2 CONT Ridefoged in Skanderborg County, living at "Oustrupgaard" at Røgen. Both the king and the sheriff have shown great youthfulness to the young rider. Due to the fact that he has received tax relief on several occasions, it may also 
2 CONC be assumed that King Frederik had the other Sejer Andersen Bonde on October 18, 1593, and on that occasion did not find the guest room and beam height in Anders Bondes old ice-cube (farmhouse) satisfactory. One fact is that when t
2 CONC he king, on November 4, is staying with the old herald attorney Peder Pedersen in. Borum exempts Sejer Bonde on "Oustrupgaard" to respond to the land guild for 3 years against Sejer on the other hand to supply the house with "good
2 CONC  buildings and comfortable rooms ".
2 CONT
2 CONT Sejer Bonde has probably not completed the conversion during the 3 years before April 16, 1587, he is committed to another year to be exempt from charges for further improving the buildings of the estate. Finally, he is released f
2 CONC or tax in March 1598, but is obliged to keep the yard in power, and must not foresee the forests belonging to the yard.
2 CONT
2 CONT Already in autumn 1598, Sejer Bonde died but no change after him was found
2 CONT
2 CONT Ridefoged at Skanderborg Castle Born approx. 1550 in Oustrupgrd, Røgen S Doped Viet 1575 Dead 06.09.1598 in Oustrupgaard Rest. 1598 in Røgen Kirke 48 years. 3 children
2 CONT photo added june2013 by Carl Madsen from Uffe Lund Sørensen website MiArv
2 CONT
2 CONT Sejer Andersen Bonde was born 1545 in Oustrupgaard, Røgen parish and died in 1598. He lived at Oustrupgaard and was riding a fighter in Skanderborg Len. Once upon a time he had visited King Frederik II, who found the ceiling heigh
2 CONC t of the farm a little low, and Sejer repeatedly received tax cuts, so he could improve the farm and ceiling height. Sejer got married to: Johanne Eriksdatter Grøn, who was born approx. 1550 at the farm Ørnhoved by Herning. She di
2 CONC ed after 1626 at Oustrupgaard. The picture: Slice of the tombstone in the church of the church of Røgen church: Johanne Eriksdatter Green and her two husbands Sejer Andersen Bonde, riding fighter in Skanderborg Len, and Jesper Ped
2 CONC ersen in honor of Gjern herred.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT http://familienbach.com/stamtra/person/1/i_I4304/sejer-andersen-bonde
2 CONT
2 CONT http://brindt.dk/erik_brindt/497.htm Ridefoged i Skanderborg len, boende paa "Oustrupgaard" ved Røgen.
2 CONT
2 CONT Both the king and the sheriff have shown great youthfulness to the young rider. because he has received tax relief several times. It may also be assumed that King Frederik, the other, had visited Sejer Andersen Bonde on 18 October
2 CONC  1593, and on that occasion did not find the guest room and beam height in Anders Bondes old ice-cube (farmhouse) satisfactory. One fact is that when the king, on November 4, is staying with the old herald attorney Peder Pedersen 
2 CONC in Borum, exempts Sejer Bonde on "Oustrupgaard" to answer the landlord for 3 years against Sejer's return to provide the house with "good buildings and comfortable rooms ".
2 CONT
2 CONT Sejer Bonde has probably not completed the conversion during the 3 years before April 16, 1587, he is committed to another year to be exempt from charges for further improving the buildings of the estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT Finally, he is released for tax in March 1598, but is obliged to keep the yard in power, and must not foresee the forests belonging to the yard.
2 CONT
2 CONT Already in autumn 1598, Sejer Bonde died but no change after him was found.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Sejer Andersen Bondo var først Rektor i Sakskøbing og i Faaborg, fra 1668 Sognepræst i Hvirring-Hornborg-Tamdrup
2 CONT
