2 CONC  Judge Jesper Pedersen, his wife, Johanne Grøn and her first husband, Sejer Andersen, Oustrup, bailiff of Headstones. 1) Half Figure stones (Fig. 31), 1616 set by former district bailiff in the works, Jesper Pedersen44 (see. P. 35
2 CONC 45) of himself, his hustru Johanne Grøn and his first husband Sejer Andersen.  The inscription mentions first Seier Andersen in Ovstrvp, formerly bailiff to Skanderborig, as 'afskildis from this vale of tears' 6 sept. 1598 and is 
2 CONC buried here with his wife Iahin (!) Green, † •. "Here at resting hindis second  hosbvnd 'Iesper Pedersen, b. In Borvm, formerly herredsfoged i Giern township, † •' oc left hand pay for oc vdhvgge this path 1616. GVD gifve dennom a
2 CONC ll one ærefvld resurrection Amen." The great and velhugne, light gray limestone, 218xl65xca. 10 cm, has a centerpiece kartoucheindrammet, rectangular box with the inscription recessed capital letters. The stone frame with slender 
2 CONC hulstavprofil the inside, carries an inscription with relief capitals from "Job 19" (v. 25): "I know that my (f) size (lev) is' etc. In the corners are circular fields with the ruling evangelists and their signs, the top Matthew a
2 CONC nd Mark (Fig. 30), the bottom Luke, and John. During a middle partitioned arcade supported by the perspective views bladvolutkonsoller shows a preparation of the above-mentioned persons. In the middle the tykkindede woman with han
2 CONC ds folded in prayer in front of the bladsmykkede  shirt. She wears konehue and round ruff of the pleated sheath. A little behind and turned against her is her two ensklædte men, with hands together put in front of the chest; their
2 CONC  pipe collars are stronger, and at the wrists discerned fine lace edges. The facial features are different; the man left, bald (?) and tapering beard, seems older than the other, with short hair and square beards. In fodfeltet fla
2 CONC nking two skulls bones of the decease bomærkeskjolde, in the middle the woman (usual) Jesus monogram "IHS", left, an arrow shaped logo on struts, right flipped four figures. - Another 189,543 were stone in korgulvet right in front
2 CONC  of the arch, later built into the choir's north wall, set in 1969 against the weapon house east wall. 
