2 CONT See Kildehenvisning, Oustrupgaard and its residents for 400 years. The estate as herred fog will be transferred to Anders Jonsen's death to Niels Jensen in Jaungyde 1 ), but the farm in Oustrup will be taken over in Henh. Formerly
2 CONC  spoken letter of life by Anders Bondes second son, Sejer An-dersen Bonde. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When Sejer Bonde, after the death of the father, does not follow this in office, but is assigned the ride as a ride-foged for a fairly extensive area of ​​the property of Skan-derborg Castle, the reason for this may be in his prob
2 CONC ably young age, because both the King and the sheriff has shown great attention to the young rider. He repeatedly receives tax relief, and the probability is that King Frederik II in the days around October 18th. 1583 has made a s
2 CONC mall visit in Oustrupgaard (well a hunting excursion). Possibly the guest room and beam height in Anders Bondes old ice-cream can not be after the king's taste, for a few days after (the 4th of November) when the king is living in
2 CONC  Borum 1 ) (well with the old herred fog over Framlev Herred, Peder Pedersen), he exonerates Sejer Bonde in Ou-strup to answer the land guild for three years, against the fact that Sejer til Gängæld will supply the farm with "Good
2 CONC  Buildings and Comfortable Rooms". 
2 CONT
2 CONT Sejer Bonde has barely finished construction work before the end of the three years, until April 16, 1587, he is promised that he may be exempt from another year's tax against further improving farm buildings with "Losementer og S
2 CONC taldrum" . And finally he is released for tax in March 1598, but is obliged to keep the farm in power and must not forgive the forests belonging to the farm. Since no further construction is required here, the buildings built by S
2 CONC ejer Bonde may have been so ample and spacious that the young Christian IV does not find grounds for making further demands. 
2 CONT
2 CONT When the "Oustrup Castle" is later talked about, this name is hardly caught out of the air. A distinctive building, Oustrup has at one time or another owned, and the conclusion is that "The Castle" is the time when Frederik II and
2 CONC  Christian IV chased in the Skanderborg Lens forests. If the "castle" was named for one of the buildings built by Sejer Bondes, or if the name - what else is supposed to be - has been linked to a kgl. hunting lodge, whose location
2 CONC  is said to have been on a west of the farm-lying terrain, can hardly be determined without digging and closer examination of the soil. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The fact that Sejer Bond's construction work has made light between the great spikes of the forest appears to be apparent from the King's above-mentioned order; but since the construction has demanded a high consumption of timber,
2 CONC  and since the supervision of the forests of the Crown did not belong to the rider's domain, but on the other hand, the forest guard Jens Mogensen in the smoke, who was tax-free at his farm in Røgen, on this point to deal with Sej
2 CONC er Bonde. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some old man has Sejer Bonde hardly been when he died in autumn 1598; but something change after him is not found. His wife's name is written on a litter in Røgen Church, and despite the imperfection of the writing, the name may b
2 CONC e found to have been Johanne Grøn. Despite the usual custom, no speeches have been reported on the spouses' children, and only by searching for Oustrup-inheritance in subsequent relatives, there have been names of some of the spou
2 CONC ses children. 
2 CONT
