2 CONT Notes: Gjøde Eriksen who were residing in Bjerregaard in Åle, born about 1500 and died before 1573. He was married to Kirsten Andersdatter born in the period 1515-1520 on Trabjerg Farm in Borbjerg Sogn. She mentioned as death in 1
2 CONC 589, she had married a second time before 1573 with Jacob Bertelsen, who inhabited Bjerregaard and since Løgagergård and later mentioned as bailiff on Silkeborg Castle. On January 7, 1552 issued the King from Queen castle is an op
2 CONC en letter that Gjøde Eriksen Bjerregaard had reported that his farm goods and all his letters on his peasant goods "are burned, then banned all to injure him or his heirs on his legal bond goods ". (Cancelliets letter books I, S. 
2 CONC 110) In 1578, conveyed Gjøde Eriksens successors part stayed associated lets and Gjøde Eriksens cousin's son, Claus Glambæk that was vasal at Skanderborg. --------------------  Erik Gødesens son Fertilize Eriksen lived in 1552 in 
2 CONC Bjerregaard, was herredsfoged and 'reckoned to the peasantry'.  Herredsfoged in Vrads-Tyrsting District, about Birth 1495 in Bjerre, Aale Sogn, four children  were residing in Bjerregaard in Åle, born about 1500 and died before 15
2 CONC 73. He was married to Kirsten Andersdatter born in the period 1515-1520 on Trabjerg Farm in Borbjerg Sogn. She mentioned as death in 1589, she had married a second time before 1573 with Jacob Bertelsen, who inhabited Bjerregaard a
2 CONC nd since Løgagergård and later mentioned as bailiff on Silkeborg Castle. On January 7, 1552 issued the King from Queen castle is an open letter that Gjøde Eriksen Bjerregaard had reported that his farm goods and all his letters on
2 CONC  his peasant goods "are burned, then banned all to injure him or his heirs on his legal bond goods ". (Cancelliets letter books I, S. 110) In 1578, conveyed Gjøde Eriksens successors part stayed associated lets and Gjøde Eriksens 
2 CONC cousin's son, Claus Glambæk that was vasal at Skanderborg ---------------- ---- Ane 1218  Gjøde E. lived in Bjerregaard in Åle, born about 1500 and died before 1573
