1 OCCU sogneprest i Tønsberg
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kapellan i Tønsberg 1651-1661, sogneprest samme sted 1661-1685.
2 CONT
2 CONT Kilde: "Nogle oplysninger om presteslekten Morland", S.H.Finne-Grønn, NST 1947
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Noter: for Sognepræst i Tønsberg Kristen Hansen Morland:
2 CONT
2 CONT Han blev uddannet på Københavns universitet som teolog og har gået på realskolen i Roskilde. Han blev kapellan i Tønsberg kirke fra 1651-1661 og var sognepræst samme sted til sin død i 1685.
2 CONT
2 CONT På den gamle Mariakirke er et vindue bevaret der står ridset Kristen Morland og et andet navn
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Parish priest in Tønsberg. Born around 1619 in Fyresdal. Died 1685.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married: Sidsel Gjertsdatter Morland (born Winge)
2 CONT
2 CONT Christen Hansson Morland Born in Fyresdal, Telemark on 1619. Christen Hansson Morland married Sidsel Gjertsdatter Winge.   He passed away on Apr 1685 in Tønsberg, Vestfold.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://leskjerv.seria.no/aner/0006/7820.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT 31/8 1663.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Morten Tygesen her sst fremlagde et afkald, hvormed '''hr Christen Hansen Morland sognepræst i Tønsberg i Norge''' giver hans svoger Morten Tygesen afkald for '''hans kæreste Sidsel Andersdatter Bondes''' arv efter hendes salig 
2 CONC far Anders Sejersen Bonde, som boede og døde i Enslev, efter skifteregister af 12-13/3 1651, og han giver sin svoger Mikkel Sørensen rådmand i Randers fuldmagt til på hans og hustru og arvingers vegne at give Morten Tygesen afkald
2 CONC  og kvittering for hendes arv, og han har bedt hans svoger Mogens Skov på Eg i Norge og Sejer Andersen Bonde studiosus theol med ham at underskrive.
2 CONT Morten Tygesen fremlagde et underskrevet afkald af hans stedsøn Sejer Anders Bonde udgivet for arv efter hans salig far Anders Sejersen Bonde, som boede og døde i Enslev, efter skifteregister 12-13/3 1651, som Morten Tygesen har v
2 CONC æret betroet, og for bondegods, som han og hans søster Sidsel Andersdatter har part og del i, som Morten Tygesen har tilforhandlet sig, og han har bedt hans morbror Mogens Skov på Eg i Norge og hans svoger '''hr Christen Hansen Mo
2 CONC rland i Tønsberg''' med ham at underskrive, og han giver hans svoger Mikkel Sørensen rådmand fuldmagt til at give hans stedfar Morten Tygesen afkald.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.brejl.dk/Bjarne/randers.html
2 CONT
2 CONT https://dis-danmark.dk/bibliotek/907035.pdf
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Anders Christensen Morland 
2 CONT * Hans Christensen Morland 
2 CONT * Susanne Helvig Christensdatter Morland 
2 CONT * Sidsel Kirstine Christensdatter Morland 
2 CONT * Ingeborg Christensdatter Morland 
2 CONT * Anne Marie Christensdatter Morland 
2 CONT * Alhed Christensdatter Morland 
2 CONT * Karen Christensdatter Morland, 1683
2 CONT * Sybille Christensdatter Morland 
2 CONT * Morten Christensen Morland
2 CONT
2 CONT ==History==
2 CONT
2 CONT We know of two churches here before the noding where built in 1843. The first church built a gong in the middle ages and torn in 1665. It was a stake church. In 1595, Bishop Jens Nilsson was on visitas in Fyresdal. He screams "---
2 CONC  Moland's church, a church of treasure, is located right at the gate of the priesthood." He shaped the church sound to improve and stop at the same church and priesthood, possibly they were not so well taken care of. Meir does not
2 CONC  win him for church.
2 CONT
2 CONT The drawings we see above are of the church that was built in 1665 and torn in 1841. Tuselikninga is from 1829 and was privately owned in 1929 when the Norwegian Folkemuseum photographed it as part of a registration work. When the
2 CONC  original car for Linaae (Linaas?) Is from, we do not know. See further under the priesthood.
2 CONT Qvisling writes that while Heggland church truleg where condemned at "the ordinary church visit" in 1668, Moland's church was all torn and built up as new years in the lead. In truely, it would be useless so that Mr. Jacob (Jacob 
2 CONC Hansen Morland was a priest 1665-1672) has been given the construction of a new church. Moland's new main church was a church church and built of timber. Procurator Lund tells of this: "A little piece from the priesthood can be se
2 CONC en as the Main Church, which is a building constructed of wood, painted without and inside, beautifully." And Wille writes: "Molands Hovedkkeke is one of the woods built in 1665, Crossroads, the most beautiful in the Upper Thelmar
2 CONC k, as it is light, net painted and emaciated with all the kings of the Oldenburg tribe straight until Frederik V."
2 CONT
2 CONT Christian VI (Photo: Olav Momrak-Haugan, 2003) In a glass gauge in a lead wind yard from this church, which later stays on a curtain in the neighborhood, it says: "H. Christen Hansen Morland. Anno1669 "He was a priest in Tønsberg 
2 CONC and was a brother of Jacob Hansen Morland who was a priest in 1665 -1672. There was more vindaugo with redeeming 1669 and name. In the crowded Moland church there is a beam from this church where it says:  THIS CHURCH WAS BECAUSE 
2 CONC OF CHRISTI 1665. J. H. S. The son of Johannes Halstein was after what is written in the call book one trunger. With this church as a model, he built in 1670 a church in Arendal. For other information he should be from Skjold in Ry
2 CONC fylke, one of the "Norwegians". However, as Qvisling writes, J. H. S. can stand for Jesus Hominus Salvator, that is, Jesus Christ's Savior.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://lokalhistoriewiki.no/wiki/Moland_kyrkje_(Fyresdal)
2 CONT
2 CONT ——————————————————
2 CONT
2 CONT The vicar Hans Jacobsen was the father of Amund Hansen (b. 1564), who was the father of Hans Amundsen Morland (1580-1643), pastor of Fyresdal in the period from 1611 to 1643 and married Susanne Arnesdatter (b. 1594 in Hobøl). Hans
2 CONC  Amundsen Morland was the father of the parish priest in Fyresdal and later Vinje Jacob Hansen Morland (1619-1698), pastor of Tonsberg Christen Hansen Morland (1619-1685), parish priest in Kviteseid and provost of Upper Telemark A
2 CONC mund Hansen Morland (1624-1700) and parish priest in Tinn (in the period 1661-1682) Werner Hansen Morland (1630-1682).
2 CONT
2 CONT Parish priest Jacob Hansen Morland was among others father of the writer in Lower Telemark Hans Morland (1677-1714). He was married to Marie Josten, daughter of bailiff in Bamble Henry Josten and sister to work victory Nils Josten
2 CONC , and then with Malene Klim, daughter of Appeal and Assessor (judge) in Over Hoff court David Klim. Christen Hansen Morland was the father of the parish priest in Aurdal and Dean Anders Christensen Morland (1666-1730), pastor of T
2 CONC onsberg Hans Christensen Morland (1669-1705) and citizen and merchant in Horsens Victory Christensen Morland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Amund Hansen Morland was first married to his predecessor's widow Johanne Madsdatter and the second time with Annie Christensdatter, daughter of Christen Andersen and Anne Gundersdatter on Borgestad Manor and widow of timber merch
2 CONC ant Samuel Halvorsen in Skien. Åse received 20 hides of goods in fatherland, and Amund Morland had a number of properties in Kviteseid and Skien. Their daughter Susanne Morland (1670-1747) was married to the priest Hans Paus, who 
2 CONC was the Morlands Chapel and subsequently succeeded as a parish priest, and as a grandchild of both Amund Morland's first spouse Johanne Madsdatter and Anne Iversdatter (married Trinepol) mentioned above. In his second marriage, Am
2 CONC und Morland was brother to lawyer Claus Andersen and uncle of Anne Clausdatter as the son-in-law Pope wrote a wisdom, and brother-in-law to Halvor Borse and Uncle of Inger Borse poison Leopoldus
2 CONT
2 CONT https://no.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Morland
